Maybe we can combine it with some kine of API design example. Something like

```c++
template<typename TAcc, typename TQueueProperty, typename TBuffer, typename TElem /* = getElementTypeFromBuffer<TBuffer */>
void gemm(alpaka::Queue<TAcc, TQueueProperty> queue, TBuffer A, TBuffer B, TBuffer C, TElem alpha, TElem beta){
// generic alpaka kernel
}

#ifdef ALPAKA_ACC_GPU_CUDA_ENABLED
template<typename TQueueProperty, typename TBuffer, typename TElem /* = getElementTypeFromBuffer<TBuffer */>
void gemm(alpaka::Queue<alpaka::AccGpuCudaRt, TQueueProperty> queue, TBuffer A, TBuffer B, TBuffer C, TElem alpha, TElem beta){
// use cuBlas
}
#endif
```

Would be pretty cool, if we have an example that shows how alpaka can be used for libraries and with specialization. This gives use also feedback, if we do API changes/extensions.

