アイコンが横一列に並んでる現状の姿は、同じ要素が同じサイズで並んでいるのでたしかに一覧性でいうと高くなりますが、操作性・この機能の重要度・機能学習してもらう手間、などを総合して判断するとデザイン原案をおすすめします。

@benfdking I created the two issues you can see above, because yesterday I was not able to find and fix them.
Therefor I fixed the other as commented above and removed the unparsable test files, so the CI should pass.
Should be ready to merge, *I hope*.

@protikbiswas100 While this does seem to implement the upstream `react-native` `tabIndex` and `focusable` Android properties (as described at https://reactnative.dev/docs/view#tabindex-android) Windows already has a `tabIndex` for Windows, which is a much more powerful (and compilcated) feature. I'm not sure the right thing to do here is to implement an Android-only property with Android-specific behavior instead of the Windows-specific behavior.

+@acoates-ms.

I think a more definitive decision needs to be made on how we implement a `tabIndex` in Fabric. On Android it looks like just an alias for `focusable`, which I don't think we need to replicate. Windows Paper customers (and maybe *all* Windows customers) will expect the fully sophisticated `tabIndex` for proper tab navigation in a Windows app.

